# Testing Conventions

Follow [`docs/engineering.md`](../../docs/engineering.md) and [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Repository assert, mock, and naming rules override portable **dotnet-test** skill defaults.

## Required

- Use **xUnit v3** (`xunit.v3` package) for all automated tests
- Use **NSubstitute** for mocks, stubs, and test doubles
- Use built-in **xUnit `Assert` methods** only
- Keep test dependencies to a minimum

## Prohibited

Do not introduce:

- FluentAssertions, AwesomeAssertions, Shouldly, Moq, NUnit, MSTest
- The `writing-mstest-tests` plugin skill (MSTest is not used here)

Do not unit-test Aspire AppHost resource modelling or orchestration.

## Conventions

- Test projects require `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>` (set in `tests/Directory.Build.props`)
- Use `[Trait("Category", "...")]` for filterable test categories (e.g. `CanonValidation`, `HugoSite`)
- Test method names may use `Method_When_Then` underscore convention (CA1707 suppressed in `tests/**/*.cs`)
- Hand-rolled fakes (e.g. `HttpMessageHandler`, `WebApplicationFactory`) are acceptable when more appropriate than NSubstitute

## Allowed supporting packages

- `bunit` — Blazor component tests
- `coverlet.collector` — code coverage
- `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing` — integration tests
- `Microsoft.Playwright` — Hugo static site browser tests (`Category=HugoSite` in `Turpinverse.Site.E2ETests`; requires built `site/public/`)
- `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk` + `xunit.runner.visualstudio` — VSTest runner

## Skills

| When | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Before running tests or quoting a `dotnet test` command | `run-tests` (`dotnet-test` plugin) |
| Uncertain test platform or MTP/VSTest mode | `platform-detection` (`dotnet-test` plugin) |
| Write, repair, or strengthen tests | `code-testing` (`dotnet-test` plugin) bound to xUnit v3, built-in `Assert`, and NSubstitute above |
| After a meaningful production change, check coverage gaps | `test-gap-analysis` (`dotnet-test` plugin) |
| Hugo site E2E or Playwright CLI workflows | `playwright-cli` (`.agents/skills/`) |